/**
@mainpage G2Basic API

G2Basic is a small BASIC interpreter written in C for microcontrollers and
other embedded hosts. A host program passes it one line at a time: numbered
lines build a stored program, and other lines run immediately. This reference
covers the public header `g2basic.h` and the internal backend hook. The source
is on [GitHub](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic).

@section mainpage_guides Guides

| Guide | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| [Language reference](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/language.md) | Statements, expressions, commands, and limits |
| [Embedding](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/embedding.md) | CMake integration, output, custom functions, and the API contract |
| [Architecture](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/architecture.md) | Parser, program store, execution, and memory |
| [Development](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/development.md) | Builds, options, tests, CI, and API documentation |
| [C coding standard](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/coding-standard.md) | Style, memory, error handling, and documentation rules |
| [Versioning](https://github.com/grzegorz-grzeda/g2basic/blob/main/docs/versioning.md) | SemVer rules, the public interface, and the changelog |

@section mainpage_groups API groups

| Group | Contents | Header |
| --- | --- | --- |
| @ref api | @ref api_setup, @ref api_functions, @ref api_execution | `g2basic.h` |
| @ref internals | @ref math_backends | `g2basic_math.h` |

The group tree is on the **Topics** page. The **Examples** page contains the
interactive interpreter, a complete host program.

@section mainpage_example Minimal host

@code
#include <stdio.h>
#include "g2basic.h"

static void print_text(const char* text) {
    fputs(text, stdout);
}

int main(void) {
    double result;
    const char* error = NULL;

    g2basic_init(print_text);
    g2basic_parse("10 FOR I = 1 TO 3", &result, &error);
    g2basic_parse("20 PRINT I, I * I", &result, &error);
    g2basic_parse("30 NEXT I", &result, &error);
    g2basic_parse("RUN", &result, &error);  // 1 1, 2 4, 3 9
    return 0;
}
@endcode
*/

/**
@defgroup internals Internal interfaces
@brief Interfaces between library sources. Host programs do not call these.
*/

/**
@example interactive/main.c
Interactive interpreter: reads lines from standard input, passes each to
g2basic_parse(), and prints error messages. Build it with the default
standalone CMake configuration and run `build/examples/interactive/g2basic-interactive`.
*/
